From 9c849dd864bcbc43058a2572d48726df5ba03937 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <services.claude@accounts.ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 09:28:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0072 -- Lever 2b -- MidiScheduler tick
 from IRQ-5 ISR

Why DOS needs this:

The 486-class campaign Bug 4 (music-tempo wobble under sub-25 fps
gameplay) traces to the engine's `MidiScheduler::tick(now_ms)` being
called from the main loop at the rendered-fps cadence. Under
FIXED_TIMESTEP (v1.0.0 default-ON), the main loop runs the 50 Hz
logic tick + an accumulator-based catch-up loop; the
MidiScheduler::tick fires once per displayed frame (~22-25 Hz on
DX2-66 heavy-music scenes). At that rate, MIDI events that should
fire at sub-40-ms granularity land late, producing operator-
perceptible tempo wobble (`docs/internal/486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md`
sec.17.3 + sec.20.4).

Lever 2b moves the MidiScheduler tick from the cooperative main-loop
path INTO the SB16 IRQ-5 ISR. The IRQ already fires at ~43 Hz under
Tier-2 (11025 Hz / 256 sample-frames), about 2x the rendered fps on
heavy-music DX2-66 scenes. The MIDI tick gains a render-rate-
independent cadence; tempo accuracy improves to ~23 ms granularity
regardless of render-fps. Structural answer to Bug 4 paralleling
Lever 3's structural answer to Bug 2.

Patch shape:

  - **New public header** `vendor/SDL/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h`
    (223 lines): standard SDL3 license + doc-comment block describing
    the engine-facing contract + the IRQ-context callback discipline
    + the killswitch shape. Declares:
      - `typedef void (*SDL_DOSMidiTickCallback)(Uint64 now_ms)` --
        the engine-implemented ISR-safe callback signature.
      - `SDL_DOSMidiTickRegister(cb)` -- engine registers / deregisters
        its callback; called once at engine init from the main thread.
      - `SDL_DOSMidiIsrTickActive(void)` -- engine-gate accessor;
        engine checks this to skip the main-loop MidiScheduler::tick
        callsite when the SDL ISR owns the tick.
    Mirrors the established public-header pattern from
    SDL_dosaudio_pump.h (SDL/0067) + SDL_dosaudio_shutdown.h
    (SDL/0053) + SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h + SDL_dospixtone.h
    (SDL/0071). Closes the "missing public header for new exported
    API" gap-class flush-instr sec.10.6 amended into the L3 design.

  - **sb.c additions** (+140 lines):
    - **Module-level state**: cached killswitch bool
      (g_dos_midi_isr_tick_active), engine callback pointer
      (g_dos_midi_tick_cb), inter-IRQ delta accumulator state
      (g_dos_midi_us_accum + g_dos_midi_last_entry_timer +
      g_dos_midi_baseline_seeded).
    - **SDL_DOSMidiTickRegister / SDL_DOSMidiIsrTickActive impls**:
      callback-pointer write is single-word aligned-volatile (atomic
      on x86; no cli/sti needed); accessor returns the cached bool.
    - **ISR insertion** at sb.c:1183-area (AFTER counter increments
      including SDL/0071's g_dos_pixtone_active_count and the existing
      doskutsu_audio_sfx_active_count, BEFORE exit_timer read at
      sb.c:1191) so the MIDI tick wall-clock cost folds into the
      existing doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us instrumentation per
      LEVER2B sec.8 Q4 + sec.10.
    - **First-IRQ-baseline-seed**: the inter-IRQ delta math is
      well-defined from the second IRQ onward; the first IRQ-post-
      engage captures the entry_timer baseline and skips the
      callback emit so subsequent emits have a valid delta source.
    - **OpenDevice hint resolution**: strict-"1" match;
      sentinel-cached on the existing pattern (matches MIDGAP_PUMP
      / TICKPUMP / DATA_CACHE / PIXTONE_PROBE / PIXTONE_IRQ_MIX).
      Two banner variants emit: ENABLED / DISABLED.
    - **DPMI locks** alongside the existing 0023+0025+0037+0038+0069
      +0071 block: DOS_LockVariable for the cached killswitch bool,
      callback pointer, inter-IRQ accumulator + last-timer +
      baseline-seeded flag.

  - **No backend-gate**. Lever 2b is orthogonal to the music backend
    choice; the engine simply doesn't register a callback when
    running under Organya (which doesn't use MidiScheduler). Under
    OPL3 (wave-46 default) / WaveBlaster / midi-stub, the engine
    registers the callback when the killswitch is engaged.

  - **OFF-path byte-identity**: when killswitch is OFF (or callback
    not registered), the new ISR hook is `if (active && cb) { ... }`
    which short-circuits to one cached-bool test + branch (~few
    cycles). Sub-microsecond per IRQ; negligible.

Engine-side responsibility (nxengine-evo/0168, not this patch):
  - Implement `extern "C"` ISR-safe shim that invokes
    MidiScheduler::tick_isr(now_ms).
  - Add tick_isr() as the ISR-context-safe variant of tick(now_ms);
    use fixed-point int64 us_per_tick_x256 (replacing the double
    `_us_per_tick`); read from a fixed-size DPMI-locked events buffer
    (replacing std::vector) per LEVER2B sec.2.
  - DPMI-lock the MidiScheduler singleton + the locked events buffer
    + the MidiBackend instance per LEVER2B sec.7.
  - cli/sti around main-thread MidiScheduler::load / start / stop /
    backend-set per LEVER2B sec.2.5.
  - Skip main-loop MidiScheduler::tick callsite when
    SDL_DOSMidiIsrTickActive() returns true.
  - Pause-coherent stop/start at game-pause transitions per
    operator choice (b) -- explicit MidiScheduler::stop at pause +
    MidiScheduler::start at unpause; ~5-10 LOC at the pause-state
    handler.

DOSBox-X smoke-gate limit per [[dosbox_not_proxy]]: DOSBox-X cannot
enforce strict DPMI page-locking; ISR-context bugs that hard-freeze
real HW often pass DOSBox-X. Lever 2b REQUIRES real-HW DX2-66
operator iter for tempo-perception validation. The banner emits at
OpenDevice and the structural correctness (callback registration +
ISR invocation cadence) is testable in DOSBox-X; the actual tempo-
accuracy improvement is real-HW-only.

Killswitch default-OFF: main-loop MidiScheduler::tick fallback path
stays alive when off so a real-HW DPMI-fault inside the registered
callback mitigates to disabled rather than freezing. Operator can
disable via the env var if any real-HW issue surfaces.

LOC: 363 insertions across 2 files (new header +223 / sb.c +140).
SDL backend only; zero engine LOC (engine work is nxengine-evo/0168).
1 new BANNERS regex entry + SEVERITY + LABEL at parity 50/50/50.
BOOT.md entry per [[env_vars_document_in_user_docs]].

Workspace-local per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md; never upstreamed.

See `docs/internal/LEVER2B-MIDI-ISR-TICK-DESIGN.md` sec.1-7 + sec.8
(Contract lock from #117/#125 STOP-and-ack closure) + sec.10.6
(public-header deliverable amendment) + 486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md
sec.17.3 + sec.20.4 (Bug 4 characterization) + `DOOM-AUDIO-
ARCHITECTURE-ANALYSIS.md` sec.5.2b (Lever 2b original spec).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
